  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Currently, the purge datastream operation allows",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "versions to be purged, but only from a specified",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "date/time backwards in the version stack. There are",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "times that it is desirable to purge just one version,",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "or purge a set of versions within a data range. One",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "important scenario is to be able to purge the most",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "recent version of a datastream to support transactional",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "activities (that may be set up in middleware above",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "Fedora). If an such a middleware transaction is being",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "managed, and middleware is required to roll back a",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "transaction, it is typically necessary to be able to",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "remove the most recent version of a datastream (given",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "that that datastream was part of the transaction). ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "Many other cases can arise where it in important to be",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "able to remove versions in a date range, for example,",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "during testing processes, where a bunch of \"junk\"",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "datastream versions get inserted in the version stack. ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "This feature is implemented by some changes to the",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "Fedora API to accomodate the start/end date range in",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "the purge operation.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
